// Figure 4.9 — Component diagram
// Eraser: New diagram > Cloud architecture (or Flow chart), paste this code.
direction right

Browser client [icon: monitor, color: orange] {
  Pages and components [icon: layout]
  Live data mirror (lib/live.ts) [icon: radio]
}

Next.js web server [icon: server, color: blue] {
  Middleware (cookie check) [icon: filter]
  Route handlers [icon: git-branch] {
    Ingest API [icon: inbox]
    Auth API [icon: lock]
    Alerts API [icon: bell]
    Reports API [icon: file-text]
    Model health API [icon: activity]
    Admin API (users / audit / threshold) [icon: settings]
    Live stream (SSE) [icon: radio]
  }
  Libraries [icon: package] {
    schemas.ts (contract + isHighRisk) [icon: file-code]
    session.ts (JWT + roles) [icon: key]
    store.ts (all SQL) [icon: database]
    scoring.ts (inference client) [icon: cpu]
    analytics.ts (pure calculations) [icon: bar-chart]
  }
}

Inference service (FastAPI) [icon: cpu, color: purple] {
  Predict endpoint [icon: zap]
  Explain endpoint [icon: search]
  Model bundle loader [icon: box]
}

Model bundles [icon: folder, color: gray]
PostgreSQL 18 [icon: database, color: green]
Transaction simulator [icon: send, color: gray]
Training scripts [icon: terminal, color: gray]

Pages and components > Route handlers: fetch / PATCH
Live data mirror (lib/live.ts) < Live stream (SSE): events
Middleware (cookie check) > Route handlers
Route handlers > Libraries
store.ts (all SQL) > PostgreSQL 18: parameterised SQL
scoring.ts (inference client) > Predict endpoint: HTTP + internal key
scoring.ts (inference client) > Explain endpoint
Model bundle loader > Model bundles: load at startup
Transaction simulator > Ingest API: HTTP + API key
Training scripts > Model bundles: write model, scaler, metadata
